-- title:
--   Adic completeness of the valuation ring of a complete valued field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field equipped with a valuation $v$ taking values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$, with the associated valued-field topology and uniformity, and assume $K$ is complete for that uniformity. Let $\varpi$ be an element of the valuation ring $\mathcal{O}[K] = \{x \in K : v(x) \le 1\}$ whose image in $K$ is non-zero, and assume the archimedean cofinality condition that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0$ with $\gamma \neq 0$ there is a natural number $n$ with $v(\varpi)^n < \gamma$. Then $\mathcal{O}[K]$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by $\varpi$: it is separated, in the sense that an element of $\mathcal{O}[K]$ lying in $(\varpi)^n \mathcal{O}[K]$ for every $n$ is zero, and it is precomplete, in the sense that every sequence $(f_n)$ in $\mathcal{O}[K]$ with $f_n \equiv f_m \pmod{(\varpi)^m}$ whenever $m \le n$ admits an element $L \in \mathcal{O}[K]$ with $L \equiv f_n \pmod{(\varpi)^n}$ for all $n$.
--
--   This is the standard comparison between the valuation filtration and the $\varpi$-adic filtration on the integers of a complete valued field: under the stated cofinality hypothesis the two filtrations are mutually cofinal, so topological completeness of $K$ transfers to $\varpi$-adic completeness of $\mathcal{O}[K]$. It is used to pass to $\varpi$-adic approximation arguments in the study of place specialisations on modular curves, for instance in the bounds on prolongation tuples for the node ring of $X_0(Nq)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Valued_isAdicComplete_integer_span_singleton_of_forall_exists_pow_lt.lean

